#
# Stand-in for the real mako-notify, which leaves the image together with sway
# and the mako daemon.
#
# This exists instead of editing the callers because there are a dozen of them
# in shared scripts (input_sense fires one on every volume and brightness step,
# start_vita3k.sh calls it with no `command -v` guard at all), and those scripts
# are built for every device, not just this one. A stub that lands only in
# gamescope images keeps sway devices untouched and turns what would be a
# "command not found" on every volume tap into a log line.
#
# On-screen notifications are a deliberate casualty of the switch, not an
# oversight - see the -no-es flag below, which the real tool used to decide
# whether EmulationStation needed pausing. Nothing here needs to pause.

logger -t mako-notify "$*"
exit 0
